# Example .encryptignore
#
# Place this file at the ROOT of a SOURCE repository to exclude files from
# encryption (and therefore from the backup). Syntax is a practical subset of
# .gitignore:
#   - blank lines and '#' comments are ignored
#   - a leading '/' anchors the pattern to the repo root
#   - '*' and '?' match within a single path segment
#   - a trailing '/' is accepted (and stripped)
#   - NOT supported: '**', negation ('!')
#
# NOTE: '.git' is always skipped automatically. Anything excluded here is NOT
# backed up, so only exclude regenerable or intentionally-unwanted files.

# Build output / dependencies (match at any depth)
node_modules/
vendor/
dist/
build/
target/

# Logs and temporary files
*.log
*.tmp

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store

# A root-level directory only (anchored)
/local-cache/
